    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature succeeds at a hostile against you.</p><hr><p><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">Fate itself seems bent to strike those who wrong you. You can choose to gain +2 circumstance bonus to damage rolls against the triggering creature on your next successful Strike or spell attack against it. If the creature critically succeeds, you gain a +4 circumstance bonus instead. This effect lasts until you make a successful strike against that creature, or until you choose another creature to use this feat against. Once you have made a successful strike against a creature with the circumstance bonus, you cannot target that creature with Karmic Retribution for 24 hours.</span></p>"
